</div></section>

<div class="rule"></div>

<section id="about">
<div class="sec-head"><h2>A mint for wasted cycles</h2><span class="num">01 — THE MINT</span></div>
<div class="two">
<div>
<p class="first">We started WastedToken Mint in a rented machine shop behind a datacenter, after a
retro where somebody totalled up the month's inference spend and the room went very quiet. That
number deserved a monument. So we cut a die for it.</p>
<p>Every coin is struck — not cast, not printed. A hardened steel die is engraved in relief, the
blank is annealed, and the press does the rest at eighty tons. The raised detail on the obverse is
metal that was pushed there, which is why the highlight rakes across it the way it does when you
turn the coin in the light.</p>
<p>Each edition is capped, numbered on the reeded edge, and retired once the last coin ships. We do
not re-strike. When a die closes we photograph it, log the final count, and shelve it next to the
others.</p>
</div>
<aside class="specs"><h3>Standard Specification</h3><dl>
<dt>Diameter</dt><dd>40.0 mm</dd><dt>Thickness</dt><dd>3.2 mm</dd><dt>Mass</dt><dd>34 g ± 0.4</dd>
<dt>Edge</dt><dd>Reeded · 140</dd><dt>Relief</dt><dd>Double-struck</dd><dt>Obverse</dt><dd>WTM emblem</dd>
<dt>Reverse</dt><dd>Denomination</dd><dt>Numbering</dt><dd>Laser, on edge</dd><dt>Case</dt><dd>Capsule + walnut</dd>
</dl></aside>
</div></section>

<div class="rule"></div>

<section id="collection">
<div class="sec-head"><h2>The collection</h2><span class="num">02 — FOUR EDITIONS</span></div>
<div class="grid">

<div class="edition" data-edition="bronze" data-state="available">
<div class="ed-top"><span class="idx">EDITION I</span><span class="tag ok">Available</span></div>
<canvas class="edition-canvas" width="420" height="420"></canvas>
<div class="ed-name">Bronze Strike</div>
<div class="ed-sub">1,000 TOKENS · 1,200 MINTED</div>
<p class="ed-desc">Warm cast bronze with an antiqued patina down in the recesses. The entry coin, and
the one people actually carry.</p>
<div class="ed-foot"><span class="price">$48</span><button class="buy">Add to cart</button></div>
</div>

<div class="edition" data-edition="silver" data-state="available">
<div class="ed-top"><span class="idx">EDITION II</span><span class="tag ok">Available</span></div>
<canvas class="edition-canvas" width="420" height="420"></canvas>
<div class="ed-name">Silver Proof</div>
<div class="ed-sub">5,000 TOKENS · 800 MINTED</div>
<p class="ed-desc">Mirror-polished fields against frosted relief. Double-struck so the emblem stands
proud of the surface.</p>
<div class="ed-foot"><span class="price">$92</span><button class="buy">Add to cart</button></div>
</div>

<div class="edition" data-edition="gold" data-state="sold-out">
<div class="ed-top"><span class="idx">EDITION III</span><span class="tag sold">SOLD OUT</span></div>
<canvas class="edition-canvas" width="420" height="420"></canvas>
<div class="ed-name">Gold Flagship</div>
<div class="ed-sub">10,000 TOKENS · 350 MINTED</div>
<p class="ed-desc">SOLD OUT — the die was retired in March. Gold over brass, the deepest relief we
have ever pressed.</p>
<div class="ed-foot"><span class="price void">$240</span><span class="locked">Die retired</span></div>
</div>

<div class="edition" data-edition="black" data-state="coming-soon">
<div class="ed-top"><span class="idx">EDITION IV</span><span class="tag soon">Minting Winter</span></div>
<canvas class="edition-canvas" width="420" height="420"></canvas>
<div class="ed-name">Obsidian</div>
<div class="ed-sub">25,000 TOKENS · 250 PLANNED</div>
<p class="ed-desc">MINTING NEXT SEASON — Winter 2026. Black PVD over steel with a polished bevel that
catches light like wet stone.</p>
<div class="ed-foot"><span class="price">$180</span><span class="locked">Winter 2026</span></div>
</div>

</div></section>

<div class="rule"></div>

<section id="process">
<div class="sec-head"><h2>How a coin gets made</h2><span class="num">03 — PROCESS</span></div>
<div class="steps">
<div class="step"><span class="n">01</span><h4>Cut the die</h4><p>The emblem is modelled in relief and
cut into hardened tool steel on a five-axis mill, then hand-stoned until the fields read as a mirror.</p></div>
<div class="step"><span class="n">02</span><h4>Strike twice</h4><p>Annealed blanks take two hits at
eighty tons. The second strike is what pushes metal fully into the deepest recesses.</p></div>
<div class="step"><span class="n">03</span><h4>Reed, number, retire</h4><p>The collar mills 140 ridges
into the edge, a laser writes the serial, and when the run completes the die is stamped void.</p></div>
</div></section>

<div class="rule"></div>

<section id="ledger">
<div class="sec-head"><h2>Provenance</h2><span class="num">04 — THE LEDGER</span></div>
<div class="two">
<div><p>Every coin leaves the shop with a printed strike card: edition, serial, die number, date of
strike, and the initials of whoever ran the press that morning. It is a shop record, and we keep the
matching copy.</p>
<p>Mail us a serial off the rim and we will tell you the exact day it was struck and what the weather
was doing, because the log sheet has a column for that and nobody has been brave enough to remove it.</p></div>
<aside class="specs"><h3>Ledger Extract</h3><dl>
<dt>Bronze Strike</dt><dd>OPEN · 1,200</dd><dt>Silver Proof</dt><dd>OPEN · 800</dd>
<dt>Gold Flagship</dt><dd>CLOSED · 350</dd><dt>Obsidian</dt><dd>WINTER 2026</dd>
<dt>Total struck</dt><dd>2,400</dd></dl></aside>
</div></section>
</main>

<footer><div class="wrap foot">
<div>© 2026 WastedToken Mint — struck in small batches, shipped worldwide.</div>
<div class="m">40MM · 3.2MM · 140 REEDS · .999 PROOF</div>
</div></footer>

